Usage: getfacl [OPTION]... FILE...

Print Windows file ACLs in a stable text format.

Options:
  -a, --access       display the access ACL (default)
  -d, --default      display the default ACL
  -R, --recursive    list ACLs recursively
  -p, --absolute-names  do not strip leading path separators
  -n, --numeric      print numeric IDs instead of account names
  -c, --omit-header  do not display the comment header
  -s, --skip-base    skip files with base ACL
  -t, --tabular      use a tabular output format

OPTIONS:
  -a, --access          display the access ACL
  -d, --default         display the default ACL
  -R, --recursive       list the ACLs of all files and directories recursively
  -p, --absolute-names  do not strip leading path separators
  -n, --numeric         print numeric IDs instead of account names
  -c, --omit-header     do not display the comment header
  -s, --skip-base       skip files that have all ACL entries equal to the base
                        ACL
  -t, --tabular         use a tabular output format
      --help            display this help and exit
  -V, --version         output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
